why Every Alliance quest of Scarlet Monastery's wings, lead-ins included.

# Scarlet Monastery's Alliance quests in one guide: Brother Crowley's chain
# through Brother Anton to Raleigh the Devout, the pick-ups in Ironforge and
# by Dalaran (for Mages their Rituals of Power chain too), the wings one after
# the other, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the
# guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The quests: Brother Crowley's 6141 Brother Anton -> 261 Down the Scarlet
# Path (thirty Undead Ravagers in Desolace) -> 1052 (to Raleigh the Devout) ->
# 1053 In the Name of the Light (Loksey, Herod, Mograine, Whitemane);
# Librarian Mae Paledust's 1050 Mythology of the Titans (in the Library);
# Magus Olvek's 96800 Past Due (The Lost Magic of the Runemasters). Mages:
# 1947 Journey to the Marsh -> Tabetha's 1949 -> Magus Tirth's 1950 -> 1951
# Rituals of Power (in the Library), and Tabetha's 1948 Items of Power -> 1952
# Mage's Wand.
#
# Left out: the Rogues' 78676 The Eye of Bhossca (its chain needs Shadowfang
# Keep); the Paladins' chain around Aeonas (79945, 79946,
# 79963, 79970), whose first quest has no giver in the data.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses or the books inside, so their
# goals stand at the monastery's door (@82.6,33.8, Tirisfal) with `group 5`.
# The wings come in the client's group finder's level order (Library 33-41,
# Armory 36-44, Cathedral 38-46; the Graveyard, 30-38, holds no Alliance
# quest), each its own instance with its own door in the courtyard, and the
# bosses in the client's dungeon journal's order within them. Every quest goal
# is counted by the quest log, so a group that takes them in another order
# still gets each step ticked. The monastery stands in Horde land.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The data has The Lost Magic of the
#   Runemasters come from an object (650929) it places nowhere.
# - The door: QuestieDB's list of Forever's dungeons, as Polestar's Codex holds it
#   (data/codex/entrances.json); the wings' own doors: runs of my own (as a
#   Horde character), each wing entered through its own door.
# - The wings and their levels: the client's group finder; the bosses: its
#   dungeon journal (as Polestar's Codex page holds it).
# - The Undead Ravagers are level 37 to 38 (data/forever); the step says so
#   rather than waiting, so a lower character can go on with the rest.
# INGAME: where in the monastery is The Lost Magic of the Runemasters?

